codex
I isolated the toolchain fault: Lean 4.22’s runtime resolves `/proc/<getpid>/exe`, while this audit sandbox exposes only `/proc/self/exe` for the process namespace. That breaks both Lean’s application-path lookup and Lake’s installation detection. I’m applying a narrow, auditable preload shim in `/tmp/audit-work` that redirects only those `/proc/<pid>/exe` `readlink` calls to `/proc/self/exe`; it does not touch the project or theorem. Then I’ll rerun the required checks under the pinned toolchain.
apply patch
