--- /dev/null
+++ b/evidence/03-independent-classification.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+INDEPENDENT CLASSIFICATION RESULT
+
+01 rule-0b30...811e  DEFINITION  madBody macro expansion naming the exact translated source body.
+02 rule-78f2...a363  DEFINITION  allFloatVS empty-sequence base equation.
+03 rule-2a5f...8e71  DEFINITION  structurally descending allFloatVS recurrence.
+04 rule-97b3...967e  DOMAIN_LEMMA  definedness characterization of the pre-existing partial Val-to-Float projection.
+05 rule-f394...403e  DEFINITION  guarded equation for fresh named proof term projectFloat.
+06 rule-004b...257  DEFINITION  reverse normalization orientation of the same fresh named proof term.
+07 rule-bd64...fbbea DEFINITION  projectFloat identity equation on the guarded Float constructor.
+08 rule-9224...e6d7  DOMAIN_LEMMA  guarded pre-existing applyBin("+") dispatch equality.
+09 rule-6f25...310f  DOMAIN_LEMMA  guarded pre-existing applyBin("-") dispatch equality.
+10 rule-07e3...bdac  DEFINITION  sumFloatVS empty-sequence fold base.
+11 rule-c262...a8ab4 DEFINITION  structurally descending sumFloatVS fold recurrence.
+12 rule-e05d...c03   DEFINITION  deviationFloatVS empty-sequence fold base.
+13 rule-86b9...e2a55 DEFINITION  structurally descending deviationFloatVS recurrence.
+14 rule-64fc...20725 DEFINITION  guarded zero-length madResult branch.
+15 rule-07a3...8ca52 DEFINITION  complementary nonzero-length madResult branch.
+
+COUNTS
+DEFINITION 12
+DOMAIN_LEMMA 3
+OPERATIONAL_RULE 0
+PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA 0
+
+SEMANTIC ANCHORS INSPECTED
+/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/operators.k:12
+  rule <k> BinOp(OP:String, L:Val, R:Val) => applyBin(OP, L, R) ... </k>
+/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:103-113
+  syntax Float ::= subF(Float, Float) [function, total, symbol(subF), no-evaluators]
+  rule subF(F1:Float, F2:Float) => F1 -Float F2 [concrete]
+  rule applyBin("-", F1:Float, F2:Float) => subF(F1, F2)
+  syntax Float ::= addF(Float, Float) [function, total, symbol(addF), no-evaluators]
+  rule addF(F1:Float, F2:Float) => F1 +Float F2 [concrete]
+  rule applyBin("+", F1:Float, F2:Float) => addF(F1, F2)
+/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k:25 and float.k:20
+  Val contains the modeled value constructors and Float is a Val.
+/reference/k-proof/verification-kompiled/definition.kore
+  isFloat is true exactly on a singleton K sequence containing an injected Float and false owise;
+  project:Float is defined exactly on that projection pattern.
+
+RELEVANCE
+The source function's first loop applies float addition, its second loop applies float subtraction followed by addition, and symbolic Val list elements require the Float projection/definedness bridge. All three domain lemmas therefore contribute directly to the source execution/postcondition. No exact rule was first proved in a rule-free module before use: prove.sh compiles the complete verification.k first and then proves spec.k, so no rule qualifies as PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA.
+
+SIMPLIFICATION POLICY
+Every rule containing a simplification or simplification(10) attribute is classified either DEFINITION (rules 5-7) or DOMAIN_LEMMA (rules 4, 8, 9).
